sts`, synthesis tries one candidate\n  with that path omitted, bounded like rule 3. `defined(note)` / `not defined(note)` both get a\n  scenario; a case asserts both.\n- Witness rule 1's doc comment states the new exception.\n- \"Absent\" vs \"present but null\" on the wire: the implementation states which the omitted\n  candidate is, in the witness module doc.\n\n## Out of Scope\n\nAbsence semantics for `==`; `when_subject` over Optional fields (#75).\n","status":"active","title":"An Optional guard is refused or witnessed as its author meant"},"lifecycle_state":"active"},"extra":null,"model_digest":"","owner":"","refs":null,"relations":null,"scope":null,"summary":"","tags":[],"title":"An Optional guard is refused or witnessed as its author meant","withholds":""},"expected_revision":3,"kind":"execute","operation":"edit","recording":{"actor":"human:timo","causation":"cmd-child-1adb95f63438e4d4a9ce1b593d20057180993525b6b64741d511b5b627977e79","correlation":"protocol-artifact-move","record_id":"aep.entity:ent-dbca744c825b0b2313edb4750f3cb488@3#0~6d4c7e4e2ab433a1","recorded_at":"2026-09-25T21:35:38Z"},"subject":["story","ent-dbca744c825b0b2313edb4750f3cb488"]}]